l of the following are true:\n\n1. Esme sits somewhere to the left of Hugo.\n2. Fitz sits in seat 1.\n3. Esme sits somewhere to the left of Ada.\n4. Fitz sits somewhere to the left of Hugo.\n5. Esme does not sit in seat 3.\n6. There are exactly 0 seats between Esme and Ada.\n\nWho sits where?\n\nGive the names in seat order from seat 1 to the last seat, separated by commas.\nReason as much as you like, then finish with one final line of the form\nANSWER: <your answer>"},{"family":"strings","id":9,"prompt":"Start with the string (between the brackets, without them): [bZkupURXLLQ12h42h]\n\nApply these steps in order:\n\n1. Keep only the characters at odd positions (the 1st, 3rd, 5th, ‚Ä¶, counting from 1).\n2. Swap the case of every letter (lowercase becomes uppercase and uppercase becomes lowercase); leave digits unchanged.\n3. Replace every occurrence of the character 2 with d (case-sensitive).\n4. Rotate the string left by 7: move its first 7 characters to the end, in the same order.\n\nWhat is the resulting string?\n\nGive the final string exactly, and nothing else after ANSWER:.\nReason as much as you like, then finish with one final line of the form\nANSWER: <your answer>"},{"family":"spec","id":10,"prompt":"Write a JavaScript function f(xs), where xs is an array of integers, that returns an integer computed as follows:\n\n1. Keep only the elements at odd indices (index 1, 3, 5, ‚Ä¶).\n2. Replace each kept element with its absolute value.\n3. Return the smallest resulting element, or -5 if there are none.\n\nReply with only the function, in a single ```js code block. Name it f, take one parameter xs, use no libraries, and write no import, require or export statements."},{"family":"logic","id":11,"prompt":"4 people (Hugo, Fitz, Bram, Cleo) sit in a row of 4 seats numbered 1 to 4 from left to right. All of the following are true:\n\n1. Bram sits in seat 3.\n2. Fitz and Cleo do not sit next to each other.\n3. There are exactly 1 seat between Hugo and Bram.\n4. Bram sits somewhere to the left of Cleo.\n5. There are exactly 1 seat between Fitz and Cleo.\n6. Cleo sits in seat 4.\n\nWho sits where?\n\nGive the names in seat order from seat 1 to the last seat, separated by commas.\nReason as much as you like, then finish with one final line of the form\nANSWER: <your answer>"},{"family":"spec","id":12,"prompt":"Write a JavaScript function f(xs), where xs is an array of integers, that returns an integer computed as follows:\n\n1. Keep every element.\n2. Replace each kept element x with 2 * x - 1.\n3. Return the smallest resulting element, or -3 if there are none.\n\nReply with only the function, in a single ```js code block. Name it f, take one parameter xs, use no libraries, and write no import, require or export statements."},{"family":"logic","id":13,"prompt":"5 people (Fitz, Ada, Hugo, Bram, Gwen) sit in a row of 5 seats numbered 1 to 5 from left to right. All of the following are true:\n\n1. There are exactly 2 seats between Hugo and Ada.\n2. There are exactly 1 seat between Hugo and Bram.\n3. There are exactly 3 seats between Hugo and Fitz.\n4. Gwen and Hugo sit next to each other.\n5. Ada sits in seat 2.\n6. There are exactly 0 seats between Gwen and Bram.\n7. Bram and Hugo do not sit next to each other.\n\nWho sits where?\n\nGive the names in seat order from seat 1 to the last seat, separated by commas.\nReason as much as you like, then finish with one final line of the form\nANSWER: <your answer>"},{"family":"strings","id":14,"prompt":"Start with the string (between the brackets, without them): [T9BTjd6RIOLEHRWNlMc5]\n\nApply these steps in order:\n\n1. Delete every 2nd character (the 2nd, 4th, 6th, ‚Ä¶ counting from 1).\n2. Keep only the characters at odd positions (the 1st, 3rd, 5th, ‚Ä¶, counting from 1).\n3. Reverse the string.\n\nWhat is the resulting string?\n\nGive the final string exactly, and nothing else after ANSWER:.\nReason as much as you like, then finish with one final line of the form\nANSWER: <your answer>